        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Aiko, Princess Toshi; Masako, Crown Princess of Japan; Crown Prince Naruhito; Emperor Akihito; Empress Michiko\n- Places: Tōgū Palace; Akasaka Estate; Akasaka, Tokyo\n- Roles: heir apparent to the Chrysanthemum Throne; official residence\n\nFacts:\n- Masako, Crown Princess of Japan, was born as Masako Owada on 9 December 1963.\n- Aiko, Princess Toshi, was born on 1 December 2001.\n- Aiko, Princess Toshi, is the only child of Crown Prince Naruhito and Crown Princess Masako of Japan.\n- Masako, Crown Princess of Japan, is the wife of Naruhito, Crown Prince of Japan.\n- Crown Prince Naruhito is the eldest son of Emperor Akihito and Empress Michiko.\n- Crown Prince Naruhito is the heir apparent to the Chrysanthemum Throne.\n- The Tōgū Palace is located in the Akasaka Estate in Akasaka, Tokyo.\n- The Tōgū Palace is the official residence of Crown Prince Naruhito, Crown Princess Masako, and their daughter Princess Toshi.",
